{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AVVwhi2apq3JwyZP8xvTQy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd096-users\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/users: Print Login Names of Currently Logged-In Users\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships users but the GNU version has consistent output formatting. The Go\n6\t  implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gusers, installed by\n7\t  coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n8\t\n9\tgoals:\n10\t  - G1: Print the login names of currently logged-in users, sorted and space-separated.\n11\t  - G2: Verify functional parity against gusers via differential testing.\n12\t\n13\trequirements:\n14\t  R1:\n15\t    title: User listing\n16\t    items:\n17\t      - R1.1:\n18\t          text: Must read the utmpx database (or equivalent on the target platform) and print the login names of all currently logged-in users on a single line, space-separated, sorted alphabetically.\n19\t      - R1.2:\n20\t          text: When given a FILE argument, must read that file as the utmpx database instead of the system default.\n21\t      - R1.3:\n22\t          text: Duplicate login names (same user logged in multiple times) must appear once per session, not deduplicated.\n23\t\n24\t  R2:\n25\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n26\t    items:\n27\t      - R2.1:\n28\t          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n29\t      - R2.2:\n30\t          text: Must exit 1 on any error.\n31\t      - R2.3:\n32\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n33\t\n34\tnon_goals:\n35\t  - cmd/users does not show idle time, terminal, or remote host information; use who for that.\n36\t\n37\tacceptance_criteria:\n38\t  - id: AC1\n39\t    criterion: \"users prints logged-in usernames sorted and space-separated, matching gusers.\"\n40\t    traces:\n41\t      - R1.1\n42\t      - R1.3\n43\t  - id: AC2\n44\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gusers passes.\"\n45\t    traces:\n46\t      - R1.1\n47\t  - id: AC3\n48\t    criterion: \"cmd/users compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n49\t    traces:\n50\t      - R1.1\n51\t      - R1.2\n52\t      - R1.3\n53\t      - R2.1\n54\t      - R2.2\n55\t      - R2.3\n56\t\n57\tpackage_contract:\n58\t  imports:\n59\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0bb1df27-2eb6-4fc4-8720-a21df565c08b","uuid":"67056340-86f6-43d9-9997-570d6a86f069","timestamp":"2026-05-24T03:23:33.869Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5569/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd096-users.yaml","content":"id: srd096-users\ntitle: \"cmd/users: Print Login Names of Currently Logged-In Users\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships users but the GNU version has consistent output formatting. The Go\n  implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gusers, installed by\n  coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the login names of currently logged-in users, sorted and space-separated.\n  - G2: Verify functional parity against gusers via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: User listing\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must read the utmpx database (or equivalent on the target platform) and print the login names of all currently logged-in users on a single line, space-separated, sorted alphabetically.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: When given a FILE argument, must read that file as the utmpx database instead of the system default.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Duplicate login names (same user logged in multiple times) must appear once per session, not deduplicated.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/users does not show idle time, terminal, or remote host information; use who for that.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"users prints logged-in usernames sorted and space-separated, matching gusers.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gusers passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"cmd/users compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}}}
