{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nwtinh4UgoLkVNCtediHWr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t//go:build darwin\n5\t\n6\tpackage sys\n7\t\n8\timport (\n9\t\t\"fmt\"\n10\t\t\"os\"\n11\t\t\"syscall\"\n12\t\t\"time\"\n13\t)\n14\t\n15\t// fileInfoFromOS extracts FileInfo from os.FileInfo using the underlying\n16\t// Darwin-specific syscall.Stat_t.\n17\t// R1.4/R2.3: handles st_mtimespec/st_atimespec/st_ctimespec naming on Darwin.\n18\tfunc fileInfoFromOS(info os.FileInfo) (*FileInfo, error) {\n19\t\tstat, ok := info.Sys().(*syscall.Stat_t)\n20\t\tif !ok {\n21\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"sys: underlying Sys() is not *syscall.Stat_t\")\n22\t\t}\n23\t\treturn &FileInfo{\n24\t\t\tMode:       info.Mode(),\n25\t\t\tSize:       stat.Size,\n26\t\t\tNlink:      uint64(stat.Nlink),\n27\t\t\tUid:        stat.Uid,\n28\t\t\tGid:        stat.Gid,\n29\t\t\tRdev:       uint64(stat.Rdev),\n30\t\t\tDev:        uint64(stat.Dev),\n31\t\t\tIno:        stat.Ino,\n32\t\t\tBlocks:     stat.Blocks,\n33\t\t\tBlksize:    int64(stat.Blksize),\n34\t\t\tModTime:    timespecToTime(stat.Mtimespec),\n35\t\t\tAccessTime: timespecToTime(stat.Atimespec),\n36\t\t\tChangeTime: timespecToTime(stat.Ctimespec),\n37\t\t\tInfo:       info,\n38\t\t}, nil\n39\t}\n40\t\n41\tfunc timespecToTime(ts syscall.Timespec) time.Time {\n42\t\treturn time.Unix(ts.Sec, ts.Nsec)\n43\t}\n44\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DAUUDFrsMbxRrZTdJaJ4jP","session_id":"0bb1df27-2eb6-4fc4-8720-a21df565c08b","uuid":"5c563ef2-af12-4f78-a640-46edfa5fe0ac","ti