{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DAUUDFrsMbxRrZTdJaJ4jP","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile the comprehensive report.\n\n## Summary of Existing cmd/ Implementations and Coding Patterns\n\nI've explored the codebase and found the following key insights:\n\n### 1. CGO Example - cmd/tty/main.go\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5569/cmd/tty/main.go`\n\nThis is the ONLY file in cmd/ that uses cgo with `import \"C\"`. It demonstrates:\n- Simple C header inclusion for `#include <unistd.h>`\n- Direct C function calls: `C.ttyname()` \n- C string conversion: `C.GoString()` for converting C strings to Go\n- Integration with pkg/sys utilities: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` and `sys.IsTerminal()`\n\n### 2. Simple cmd/ Pattern Examples\nAll other commands follow a consistent, simple pattern without cgo. Examples:\n\n**cmd/whoami/main.go** - Minimal implementation\n- Uses standard Go packages only (os, os/user)\n- Single function: `parseFlags()` for argument parsing\n- Calls `os.Exit()` with appropriate codes (0, 1)\n- Uses `fmt.Fprintln()` and `fmt.Fprintf()` for output\n- Help and version text as module-level constants\n\n**cmd/logname/main.go** - Similar structure\n- Gets environment variable: `os.Getenv(\"LOGNAME\")`\n- Error handling with exit codes\n- Same argument parsing pattern\n\n**cmd/pwd/main.go** - More complex flag handling\n- Multiple modes (logical/physical)\n- Short flags: `-L`, `-P` and long flags: `--logical`, `--physical`\n- Separate flag parsing functions: `parseArgs()` and `parseShortFlags()`\n- Helper functions for core logic: `physicalDir()`, `logicalDir()`, `isValidLogicalPWD()`\n\n### 3. No cmd/who/ Implementation Found\nThe `cmd/who/` directory does not exist in this repository. This is expected since it will be a new implementation you're working on.\n\n### 4. pkg/sys/ Utilities Available\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5569/pkg/sys/`\n\nKey utilities you should use:\n- **sigpipe.go**: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - Installs SIGPIPE handler that exits 0 (used in all main functions)\n- **terminal.go**: \n  - `sys.IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool` - Check if fd is a terminal\n  - `sys.TerminalWidth() (int, error)` - Get terminal width via TIOCGWINSZ ioctl\n- **fileinfo.go**: `sys.Stat()` and `sys.Lstat()` - Extended file metadata\n- **signal.go**: `sys.OnTerminalResize()` - Register SIGWINCH callbacks\n- **stat_darwin.go**: Platform-specific Stat_t handling for Darwin (uses `//go:build darwin` tags)\n\n### 5. Common Coding Patterns\nAll cmd/ implementations follow these patterns:\n1. Copyright header and SPDX identifier\n2. Package main with implementation reference comment\n3. Help and version text as constants\n4. Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` in main()\n5. Parse arguments from `os.Args[1:]`\n6. Use `os.Exit()` with appropriate exit codes\n7. Write to stderr for errors, stdout for normal output\n8. Support `--help`, `--version`, `--`, and unrecognized option error messages\n\nThe codebase is well-structured and follows POSIX specification references (like \"srd042-whoami R1.1\" in whoami/main.go)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0bb1df27-2eb6-4fc4-8720-a21df565c08b","uuid":"9e8ff77f-972b-4a7f-88a2-c09eb7aaf273","timestamp":"2026-05-24T03:25:06.138Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5569, I need to see existing cmd/ implementations to understand the coding style and patterns used. Show me:\n\n1. A simple cmd/ main.go that uses cgo (if any exist) - search for `import \"C\"` in cmd/\n2. If no cgo examples, show me 2-3 simple cmd/ main.go files (like cmd/yes/main.go, cmd/whoami/main.go, cmd/logname/main.go, cmd/tty/main.go, or cmd/nohup/main.g